# The pcache entries use a claim-protocol write (key0 claim, key1
# last) and a validating read (the 128-bit key snapshot, then the
# atomic ACQUIRE value loads only after the key match). The 128-bit
# key snapshot races the writer by design; a torn or stale snapshot
# fails the match and the probe continues, so the access is
# deliberate. Everything else TSan reports on these paths is a real
# finding.
race:tsimd_pcache_probe_serve
race:tsimd_pcache_probe_merged
race:tsimd_pcache_probe_merged_ns
